From 64ebe3727ee622f921d68c21ccebfd4089b673f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:17:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] List section planets from one density clustering.

cluster_once assigns each planet to the section that holds most of its
posts, lists it in both when the top two are each at least 35%, and
reuses one set of labels. A section that publishes fewer than 10 planets
is clustered on its own to fill the rest. The 10K comparison fills every
section with fewer label calls than re-clustering each section, so
cluster_once is the default.

Not applied on the #85 branch. `git apply` this file on top of the
density-grouping tree whose spec points here. The natural-grouping.md
hunk context matches that pointer sentence.

Co-authored-by: Michael Link <Data-Science-Link@users.noreply.github.com>
