diff --git a/.factory/DECISIONS.md b/.factory/DECISIONS.md
index ad1f90f..60ceeac 100644
--- a/.factory/DECISIONS.md
+++ b/.factory/DECISIONS.md
@@ -236,3 +236,9 @@ Append-only. Newest at the bottom.
 - **Why:** A formula for the cell count was deciding how many topics existed before the posts were read. About 200 cells at 10K, then a floor of `n // 200`, left 12 candidates and 85.8% of posts as noise. On this embedding a topic is a ball of posts near one center. Single-linkage on mutual reachability, the HDBSCAN distance, was measured and does not separate the week: nearest-neighbor distances inside a topic and between topics are almost the same, so the graph becomes one chain (one group of about 2,800 posts and a handful of specks). The ball count stays near 250–270 at floor 8 when the grid moves from 800 to 1,600 seeds, so the grid is not the answer.
 - **Alternatives:** Lower the k-means floor and publish `k = n / floor` cells. Keep single-linkage anyway. Build an n×k distance matrix at 100K.
 - **Revisit when:** A 10K week produces only a handful of candidates, the share of posts in a group falls back near 14%, or a 100K run cannot finish the sample-and-assign path in about 10 minutes.
+
+### 2026-10-08 — List planets from one clustering; re-cluster a section only to fill it (#85, #32)
+- **Decision:** `section_grouping` defaults to `cluster_once`. One density pass produces the planets. Each planet is listed in the section that holds the most of its posts. When the top two sections are each at least 35% of the planet, it is listed in both. Rank is still distinct authors, then size, and each section shows its top 10. A planet is labeled once and that label is reused in the global list and every section list. A section that publishes fewer than 10 planets is clustered on its own, and those planets fill the empty slots. `per_section` remains the setting that clusters every section again. This does not replace the Jev-per-planet section call in [2026-10-08 — Group once; Jev picks the section per planet, not per post (#90, #87)](#2026-10-08-group-once-jev-picks-the-section-per-planet-not-per-post-90-87). That call still waits on its shadow test. The comparison is in `docs/research/natural-grouping.md`.
+- **Why:** On the 10K artifact, cluster-once filled all 10 sections (the Sports fallback added two planets), all 10 global planets also appeared in a section, and the labeler had 100 planets / 175 faces / about 725 calls. Re-clustering every section had 110 planets / 192 faces / about 796 calls, and one global planet did not show up in any section list. Both projections sit under 20 minutes (about 567s and about 612s).
+- **Alternatives:** Keep re-clustering every section (`per_section`). Wait for the #90 Jev-per-planet shadow test before changing section lists at all.
+- **Revisit when:** A section’s top 10 is full of planets whose posts are mostly another section, the fallback runs for most sections, or the #90 shadow test replaces this majority rule with a Jev call per planet.
